<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Adolf I, Prince of Schwarzenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1615–1683</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Johann Adolf von Schwarzenberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Adolf I was the first prince of Schwarzenberg, a senior adviser of Emperor Leopold I and president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulic-council">Imperial Aulic Council</a>. In 1670 he was raised to the rank of prince of the Empire, with the family's Franconian lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheinfeld">Scheinfeld</a> forming the core of the principality. He also acquired large estates in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, laying the basis of the family's later wealth in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-adolf-i-prince-of-schwarzenberg.jpg" alt="Johann Adolf I, Prince of Schwarzenberg" width="320" height="557" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean-Adolphe_de_Schwarzenberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
